            <ArticleTitle>Gynecologic aspects of the &quot;routine&quot; checkup.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>164-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A Pap test, advice about contraception, and instruction in breast self-examination--these are important components in the routine physical checkup of female patients. The practice of office gynecology is a demanding but rewarding part of general medical practice.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
